+# Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Todos get an optional `dueDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) plus a computed `overdue` flag, a `?overdue=` filter, and the list page shows both with a „nur überfällige“ toggle.
+
+**Architecture:** All domain logic lives in `src/store.mjs`: `createStore({ today })` validates/stores `dueDate` and returns copies with `overdue` computed against an injectable UTC clock. `src/app.mjs` only parses the `overdue` query parameter. `public/index.html` renders the API fields; it never computes overdue itself.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Node 24, `node:http`, `node:test`, plain HTML/JS — zero dependencies.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-14-faelligkeitsdatum-design.md` (Ticket #1)
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- Zero dependencies — Node builtins only.
+- Validation errors are `ValidationError` from `src/store.mjs` → HTTP 400.
+- `dueDate` error message: `dueDate must be a valid date (YYYY-MM-DD) or null`.
+- Filter error message: `overdue must be true or false`.
+- Overdue = `!done && dueDate !== null && dueDate < today()`; `today()` returns the UTC date `YYYY-MM-DD`, default `new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10)`.
+- Every UI element tests rely on has a `data-testid`: new ones are `filter-overdue`, `todo-due`, `todo-overdue`.
+- UI copy, exact: `nur überfällige`, `fällig: <YYYY-MM-DD>`, `überfällig`.
+- TDD: failing test first.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+1. A PATCH with one invalid field (e.g. valid `title` + invalid `dueDate`) must leave the todo completely unchanged — today `update` mutates `title` before validating `done`. Validate all fields first, then apply. (Test in Task 1.)
+2. Overdue is re-evaluated on every read: marking an overdue todo `done: true` clears `overdue`, setting it back to `false` restores it. (Test in Task 1.)
+3. Mutating an object returned by the store must not change stored state (copies, not internal objects), and stored todos never contain an `overdue` property. (Test in Task 1.)
+4. `?overdue=` (empty) and `?overdue=TRUE` are rejected with 400, not treated as "no filter". (Test in Task 2.)
+5. Leap-year check must not rely on `Date.UTC` for years < 100 (JS maps them to 19xx); use arithmetic: leap = `y % 4 === 0 && (y % 100 !== 0 || y % 400 === 0)`. (Test in Task 1: `'2000-02-29'` valid, `'1900-02-29'` invalid.)
+
+---
+
+### Task 1: Store — `dueDate`, `overdue`, filtered `list`
+
+**Files:**
+- Modify: `src/store.mjs`
+- Test: `test/store.test.mjs` (create)
+
+**Interfaces:**
+- Produces:
+  - `createStore({ today } = {})` — `today: () => string` (`YYYY-MM-DD`, UTC), optional.
+  - Todo shape returned by `list`, `get`, `add`, `update`: `{ id, title, done, dueDate: string|null, overdue: boolean }` — always a fresh copy.
+  - `list({ overdue } = {})` — `overdue: boolean|undefined`; undefined → all todos.
+  - `add({ title, dueDate })`, `update(id, patch)` — `dueDate` absent/`null`/valid string; otherwise `ValidationError` with the constant message.
+
